          "text": "Cuba was never and is never going to be China. China has 1.5 billion ppl. At the start of reform and opening-up it had 900 million and about 15% of an entire continent. For Cuba to be like China it would need to join mainland America or vice-versa(There is a history with the US and Mexico but I do not want to be labor the point but there is prior understanding). High-speed rail, or even light-rail, a bunch of cars,  a bunch of factories to expand the point also is not viable.",
